WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.591
Data control is a common reason for local inference.

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:14.873
Prompts and outputs can remain within an approved environment when the application, logs, interfaces, and supporting tools are configured accordingly.

00:00:14.953 --> 00:00:18.523
Local execution does not automatically prevent leakage.

00:00:18.603 --> 00:00:25.234
Offline capability can support field work, isolated labs, unreliable connectivity, or continuity needs.

00:00:25.314 --> 00:00:36.026
The model, runtime, dependencies, documentation, and required reference data must already be available and maintained for offline use to be meaningful.

00:00:36.106 --> 00:00:42.227
Local systems support experimentation with model families, quantizations, prompts, adapters, and runtimes.

00:00:42.307 --> 00:00:54.549
Teams can inspect performance and behavior without every request becoming a metered external call, although hardware, electricity, engineering time, and maintenance still have cost.

00:00:54.629 --> 00:01:04.321
Customization may include retrieval over approved data, structured workflows, domain prompts, fine-tuned or adapted models, and local integrations.

00:01:04.401 --> 00:01:08.992
Each change creates evaluation, security, provenance, and lifecycle responsibilities.

00:01:09.072 --> 00:01:17.233
Hosted models may offer stronger capability, larger context, managed scaling, rapid updates, and less infrastructure work.

00:01:17.313 --> 00:01:27.005
Local models may have lower quality on difficult tasks, limited concurrency, hardware constraints, and slower access to new capabilities.

00:01:27.085 --> 00:01:34.736
Choose local when its control, latency, offline, integration, or economic benefits match a real requirement.

00:01:34.816 --> 00:01:42.977
Do not choose it solely to avoid governance or because hardware ownership feels equivalent to privacy.

00:01:43.057 --> 00:01:45.608
Hybrid approaches are often practical.
